0.0},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 9 daily record highs, no daily record lows","records":"Merced has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"Merced has warmed, days and nights alike","rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 71\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>71\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 67\u00b0F, and the record is 84\u00b0F (1900). The low of <strong>49\u00b0F</strong> was the 15th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 126 since 1899.","t_rec":"Merced has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Merced's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Merced has set <strong class=\"sig\">12 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 80 that chance alone would give, and <strong>97 record highs</strong>, close to the 80 that chance alone would give. The 1900s hold the most record highs of any decade (66). Merced's all-time high is 116\u00b0F, on September 6, 2022.","t_chg":"Merced has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 101 complete years: Merced's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.21\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.14 to +0.29), about +2.6\u00b0F since 1902. Merced's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.13\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.06 to +0.21), about +1.7\u00b0F since 1902.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 10 of 12 months. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Merced's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.04 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 11.8 inches a year. The wettest year was 1998 (21.98 in); the driest, 2013 (3.79 in). Merced almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 9 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}